A||||3||Green Meanie||Parking Space Blues...
Z||000000||Green Meanie||07-09-99||12:09 AM||||1985 Fiero GT 40 over is having trouble getting out of it's parking space.<br>I ran it on the highway where it was bucking a little on me, and had been doing so for a day or two.  Then when I got off the highway, I had no power, and the car would not rev up, and it was back firing like crazy.  I managed to get 'er home, but now that it's in the parking space, it will only run for a few minutes where after that it stalls.<p>Can anyone either relate to this, or does anyone have any suggestions on where to start looking?  Or should I just start attending church more often and hope for a miracle??!<p>Thanks,<p>Green Meanie!
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||07-09-99||02:21 AM||||My first guess would be the ignition module. It's not an all too expensive part and replacing an old one is always a good idea... But before you replace it, try the following first:<p>- Disconnect the tachfilter and see if it still has the problem.<br>- Check the sparkplug wires for cracks. Replace them anyway.<br>- If problem still remains, replace ignition module.<p>Hope this helps.
Z||000002||Carrolles||07-09-99||06:56 AM||||Take a look at your catalitic converter also.
Z||000003||burdell1||07-09-99||08:36 AM||||I had a similar problem recently. It turned out to be a bad fuel pump. 
